I've got a fairly simple file that shows a high degree of non-determinism when run.  (Maya 2009-x64 on CentOS 5.4, Bullet 2.76.)  It's a shattered object, with the individual pieces having initial pos/rot/vel/spin set, plus a ground plane.  I didn't see an option in the solver for randomization - perhaps it's not exposed?<br><br>Is there something I'm missing?  I was under the impression that Bullet was deterministic.  Is there something else I need to do to reset the solver between successive runs?  File is attached - run it multiple times, and watch where the pieces end up... not even remotely in the same position.<dl class="file"><dt><span class="imageset icon_topic_attach"></span> <a class="postlink" href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=448">testBullet2.tgz</a></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6428">meeotch</a> — Fri Mar 12, 2010 10:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
